 {
  "kind": "text",
  "text": "I built the reveal as a 7-second, 1080×1920 composition on a near-black background (#0B0A09) with ivory and champagne-gold type.\n\n- **Gold line** (**Gold line**): a 1.5 px champagne rule draws outward from its center over 0.3–2.7 s, with Sine In Out easing.\n- **Name** (**Name ÉCLAT**, split into five letter layers): each letter fades in from 0 over about 1.2 s, staggered 0.25 s from 1.6 s to 2.6 s. Each letter also slides inward, from about 12% wider than its final spot to its place, with Quart Out. That is how I got the tracking tightening, since the tool can't animate tracking directly.\n- **Subline** (**Subline**): \"Eau de Parfum\" in gold italic-free serif fades in and rises a few pixels from 4.6 s to 5.8 s.\n- **Hold**: everything rests from about 5.8 s to the end, so the final frame is the full lockup.\n\nNothing moves faster than about 1.2 s per move. The critic scored it 71/100. I left two of its notes unapplied:\n- It wants overshoot or idle motion. I left them out because you asked for restrained, and a breathing or overshoot effect would work against that.\n- It flagged the letter slides as sluggish. I kept them slow on purpose, since you said nothing should move fast.\n\nThe typeface is a caveat: Cormorant Garamond isn't installed here, so the name and subline render in the system serif. If you have a licensed wide-tracked serif (Cormorant, Bodoni, or Didot-style), tell me its name and I'll swap it in.\n\nNext steps I could take: add a soft gold glow or grain behind the name, add a slow push-in across the hold, or export a preview.",
  "at": 1794513166386
 },
